  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-33540",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/distribution/distribution: Distribution: Information disclosure via improper validation of authentication realm URL"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Distribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.0, in pull-through cache mode, distribution discovers token auth endpoints by parsing WWW-Authenticate challenges returned by the configured upstream registry. The realm URL from a bearer challenge is used without validating that it matches the upstream registry host. As a result, an attacker-controlled upstream (or an attacker with MitM position to the upstream) can cause distribution to send the configured upstream credentials via basic auth to an attacker-controlled realm URL. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.1.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33540",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-33540\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/distribution/distribution/v3\nFixed Version: 3.1.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-33540](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33540)\nDistribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.0, in pull-through cache mode, distribution discovers token auth endpoints by parsing WWW-Authenticate challenges returned by the configured upstream registry. The realm URL from a bearer challenge is used without validating that it matches the upstream registry host. As a result, an attacker-controlled upstream (or an attacker with MitM position to the upstream) can cause distribution to send the configured upstream credentials via basic auth to an attacker-controlled realm URL. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.1.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-33540**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/distribution/distribution/v3|3.1.0|[CVE-2026-33540](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33540)|\n\nDistribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.0, in pull-through cache mode, distribution discovers token auth endpoints by parsing WWW-Authenticate challenges returned by the configured upstream registry. The realm URL from a bearer challenge is used without validating that it matches the upstream registry host. As a result, an attacker-controlled upstream (or an attacker with MitM position to the upstream) can cause distribution to send the configured upstream credentials via basic auth to an attacker-controlled realm URL. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.1.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-35172",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/distribution/distribution: Distribution: Information disclosure via stale references after content deletion"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Distribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.0, distribution can restore read access in repo a after an explicit delete when storage.cache.blobdescriptor: redis and storage.delete.enabled: true are both enabled. The delete path clears the shared digest descriptor but leaves stale repo-scoped membership behind, so a later Stat or Get from repo b repopulates the shared descriptor and makes the deleted blob readable from repo a again. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.1.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-35172",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-35172\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/distribution/distribution/v3\nFixed Version: 3.1.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-35172](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-35172)\nDistribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.0, distribution can restore read access in repo a after an explicit delete when storage.cache.blobdescriptor: redis and storage.delete.enabled: true are both enabled. The delete path clears the shared digest descriptor but leaves stale repo-scoped membership behind, so a later Stat or Get from repo b repopulates the shared descriptor and makes the deleted blob readable from repo a again. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.1.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-35172**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/distribution/distribution/v3|3.1.0|[CVE-2026-35172](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-35172)|\n\nDistribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.0, distribution can restore read access in repo a after an explicit delete when storage.cache.blobdescriptor: redis and storage.delete.enabled: true are both enabled. The delete path clears the shared digest descriptor but leaves stale repo-scoped membership behind, so a later Stat or Get from repo b repopulates the shared descriptor and makes the deleted blob readable from repo a again. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.1.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
