            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41888",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/distribution/distribution: Distribution: Security bypass allows unauthorized tag deletion"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Distribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.1, tag deletion via the DELETE /v2/\u003cname\u003e/manifests/\u003ctag\u003e endpoint bypasses the storage.delete.enabled: false configuration, allowing any API client to remove tags from repositories even when the operator has explicitly disabled deletion. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41888",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41888\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/distribution/distribution/v3\nFixed Version: 3.1.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-41888](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41888)\nDistribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.1, tag deletion via the DELETE /v2/\u003cname\u003e/manifests/\u003ctag\u003e endpoint bypasses the storage.delete.enabled: false configuration, allowing any API client to remove tags from repositories even when the operator has explicitly disabled deletion. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.1.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41888**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/distribution/distribution/v3|3.1.1|[CVE-2026-41888](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41888)|\n\nDistribution is a toolkit to pack, ship, store, and deliver container content. Prior to 3.1.1, tag deletion via the DELETE /v2/\u003cname\u003e/manifests/\u003ctag\u003e endpoint bypasses the storage.delete.enabled: false configuration, allowing any API client to remove tags from repositories even when the operator has explicitly disabled deletion. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.1.1."
              },
              "properties": {
